      "additional_results": "Uniform exact first-hit coefficient bound at positive odd targets, including periodic targets; actual finite cylinder-mass transport and energy decomposition; an exact finite-energy criterion equivalent to universal eventual periodicity, with unconditional normalized decay outside every diverging ancestor barrier. Unconditional raw occupation lower bound: for every b<1/log(4/3), the sum of actual weighted first-hit densities over odd N\u2264R is at least b log R for all sufficiently large integer R. A specified injective odd orbit forces the additional lower coefficient D_u/(P_infinity(u)*log(3/2)), strictly positive at unit roots. Under the actual inverse Doob law at every positive odd nonperiodic unit root, log(Y_k)/k tends almost surely to log(4/3).",
      "credit": "The inverse-linear form was proposed by Wirsching. The proof uses Mazur's weighted predecessor construction and Said Duran's coalescence theorem, alongside the density and canonical-limit foundations described in the paper.",
      "main_result": "For one fixed positive integer K_seed and every positive target N prime to three, shortcut and ordinary predecessor natural densities are at least 3/(128*K_seed*N).",
      "numbered_results": 31,
      "pages": 37,
      "pdf": "paper/tao-basin-densities.pdf",
