      "title": "Collatz basin densities and canonical traces from first-passage stabilization"
    },
    {
      "additional_results": "Conditioning on total-exponent slices with polynomially bounded reciprocal mass preserves superpolynomial decay for n-k<=k^beta, 0<beta<1. The central slice S_k=2k has mass at least 1/(4k) for k>=1 and satisfies that decay conclusion for k>=4.",
      "credit": "Tao's full-length endpoint is prior work. The comparison with Si is confined to his stated central-slice logarithmic oversampling range. The proof incorporates the credited Subspace Theorem formalizations and renewal inputs.",
      "limitations": "Constants are ineffective. No conductor-power decay at fixed positive deficit ratio, deterministic integer transfer, or Collatz convergence result is asserted.",
      "main_result": "For every fixed natural A, primitive Fourier coefficients of the k-step geometric Syracuse affine law modulo 3^n are bounded by C_A*((n-k+2)/n)^A for n>=1 and 0<=k<=n, uniformly in the seed and in unit-modulus phases depending on the total exponent.",
      "numbered_results": 6,
      "pages": 9,
      "pdf": "paper/growing-deficit-fourier.pdf",
      "pdf_sha256": "c4cef4da6a990d118fab44e9086f4ed59882b9012b8175952fe22b73174c0222",
      "source": "paper/growing-deficit-fourier.tex",
