      "title": "Fourier decay for truncated Syracuse affine laws"
    },
    {
      "additional_results": "Uniform finite-level Lp bounds for every real 1<=p<2; the actual stationary density equation; failure of L2 through positive support overlap. The depth-zero and p=1 finite-level boundary cases are assembled from the named public endpoints explained in the theorem map.",
      "credit": "Tao supplies the random law, fine-scale mixing and fixed-length/fixed-total offset injectivity. The quadratic energy argument uses distinct natural quotients and normalized geometric moments. No exhaustive priority claim is made.",
      "limitations": "These are random-law Haar estimates. No weak-L2 bound, exact linear energy growth, integer trace estimate or individual-orbit convergence result is asserted.",
      "main_result": "For the canonical fair Syracuse law on the 3-adic integers, full-Haar depth-k cylinder energy is at most 24k+8k^2<=32k^2 for k>=1. One normalized nonnegative density has exact real Lp range 1<=p<2.",
